/*--------------------------------------------

 Thin Lens - Polycarbonate (advanced materials demo)

 A thin lens has no radii or media to name, so it takes a material directly: the power typed
 is for the d line (587.6 nm) and scales with (n - 1) at other wavelengths. Polycarbonate
 (Abbe number about 30) is a deliberately dispersive spectacle material - switch the
 wavelength between F and C and watch the focus move. Set the material to "Fused silica"
 or to nothing at all and the shift shrinks or disappears.

----------------------------------------------*/

